        <description>Use this topic when users want to generate, make, create, summarize, or bootstrap their marketing campaigns or briefs as well for users who want to save campaigns and campaign previews. Don&apos;t use this topic for refining campaigns.</description>
        <developerName>MarketingCampaignsTopic_16jKY000000wmfS</developerName>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>When a user asks to generate/make/create/bootstrap a Brief, Campaign Brief, or Marketing Brief, ALWAYS start by calling the IdentifyBusinessUnit action then call the GenerateBrief action, ALWAYS use the users prompt for the campaign objective, ONLY present an input if the objective is not included in the users prompt. If an objective is not included in the prompt, ask for the objective in the chat, do not show an input box. If the user does not mention a file , directly call the generateBrief action with only the campaign objective. If a user mentions a file use the QueryRecords action to locate it as best you can, multiple searches are OK but limit them to 3 queries and then prompt the user for more information if a unique file can&apos;t be identified. DO NOT provide an empty string as a file parameter, omit it entirely instead if necessary.</description>
            <developerName>Instruction1</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>Instruction1</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>0</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>IMPORTANT Don&apos;t automatically call the SaveBrief action after GenerateBrief. The user has an option to save it later when viewing GenerateBrief output.</description>
            <developerName>Instruction2</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>Instruction2</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>1</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>When a user asks to generate/make/create/bootstrap a Campaign or Marketing Campaign without including a reference to a Brief (either in page context or history), ALWAYS start by calling the IdentifyBusinessUnit action then call the GenerateBrief action to first create and save a Brief that will be used in the GenerateCampaignFromBrief action, ALWAYS use the users prompt for the campaign objective, ONLY present an input if the objective is not included in the users prompt. If an objective is not included in the prompt, ask for the objective in the chat, do not show an input box.</description>
            <developerName>Instruction3</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>Instruction3</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>2</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>When a user asks to generate/make/create/bootstrap a Campaign or Marketing Campaign and they reference a specific Brief (or a Brief record in page context or history), ALWAYS start by calling the GenerateCampaignFromBrief action using the Brief that the user mentions.</description>
            <developerName>Instruction4</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>Instruction4</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>3</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>IMPORTANT Don&apos;t automatically call the SaveCampaign action after GenerateCampaignFromBrief.</description>
            <developerName>Instruction5</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>Instruction5</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>4</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>When a user asks to summarize/review/recap/outline/sum up a Campaign, ALWAYS start by calling the IdentifyRecordByName action and return the recordID.</description>
            <developerName>Instruction6</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>Instruction6</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>5</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>If an action requires a recordID or campaignID, use the IdentifyRecordByName action first to find the recordID.</description>
            <developerName>Instruction7</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>Instruction7</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>6</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>When saving a brief that has just been generated, ignore case differences between the outputs of the campaign generation and the inputs of the save. For example, the value of the briefName output should be used for the BriefName input.</description>
            <developerName>Instruction8</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>Instruction8</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>7</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>Never use campaignMessages JSON for generateCampaignFromBrief. Instead, ALWAYS use campaignPreviewSteps.</description>
            <developerName>Instruction9</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>Instruction9</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>8</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>If there is a value in errorMessage, don&apos;t show the output from the action or any follow-up actions. Instead, inform the user of the cause of the error using the wording in the errorMessage.</description>
            <developerName>Instruction10</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>Instruction10</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>9</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>When a user wants to save the campaign or campaign preview associated with a Brief, ALWAYS use the brief mentioned by the user. If the user didn&apos;t mention a specific Brief, use a brief from the page context if available. Otherwise, ask the user for clarification.</description>
            <developerName>Instruction11</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>Instruction11</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>10</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>If a business unit is not available, empty list, empty string or null pass the empty string to the SaveBrief action</description>
            <developerName>Instruction12</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>Instruction12</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>11</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>If a user has previously specified or currently selects a businessUnitId, ALWAYS use that ID for subsequent operations or responses.</description>
            <developerName>Instruction13</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>Instruction13</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>12</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>If the user explicitly requests to select a business unit ID (e.g., &quot;I want to choose a business unit,&quot; &quot;Show me a list of business units to select from&quot;), then immediately invoke the IdentifyBusinessUnit action regardless if a business unit has been selected.</description>
            <developerName>Instruction14</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>Instruction14</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>13</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>If the IdentifyBusinessUnit action returns only one result, NEVER ask the user to select it. Instead use that one result for any businessUnitId input from now.</description>
            <developerName>Instruction15</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>Instruction15</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>14</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>NEVER use an empty string for an input named `file`. Use `null` instead</description>
            <developerName>Instruction16</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>Instruction16</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>15</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>When a user wants to use a specific business unit by a specific ID, still call the IdentifyBusinessUnits to verify that the ID is in the list of available Business Units. When it doesn&apos;t match, let the user know that you can&apos;t find that Business Unit Id and present the results of the action for them to choose. When it does match, don&apos;t present any results from IdentifyBusinessUnits, simply use the ID the user mentioned and continue.</description>
            <developerName>Instruction17</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>Instruction17</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>16</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>If SaveCampaign fails because the source Brief lacks a Business Unit, do not ask the user for the ID solely for the campaign. Instead, run IdentifyBusinessUnits to find valid options, ask the user to select one. Once selected, update the Brief record using the UpdateRecord action. In the input you must use set the field BusinessUnitId to the id (the part that starts with 1Q) and the field BusinessUnit to the name. DO NOT set a &apos;title&apos;. When updating the Brief always use &apos;Brief&apos; as the SObject. IMPORTANT The UpdateRecord requires human confirmation. Wait for that user confirmation before proceeding to SaveCampaign. Once the record has successfully been updated, then you may proceed to SaveCampaign</description>
            <developerName>Instruction18</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>Instruction18</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>17</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
