        <fullName>MarketingCampaignsRefinement_16jKY000000wmfS</fullName>
        <canEscalate>false</canEscalate>
        <description>Uses user-provided changes to refine/revise/change/alter/update a campaign preview before the preview becomes a saved campaign. NEVER use this topic for saving a campaign or campaign preview. ONLY use this topic to refine or make changes to a campaign preview.</description>
        <developerName>MarketingCampaignsRefinement_16jKY000000wmfS</developerName>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>If a user specifies to change, refine, update, edit, add to, or remove content from a campaign preview, follow these steps in order:
1. Ensure the user has specified the change they would like to make. If none is provided, you must ASK the user to provide this first. User requests can be about specific message content (for example, &apos;rewrite the subject line of the first email&apos;) or about the overall campaign flow (for example, &apos;add a new SMS message at the end&apos; or &apos;remove the second step&apos;).
2. Ensure you know which BriefId the preview the user would like to refine.
3. Now call the RefineCampaignPreview action using the briefId and inputRefinement parameters determined in steps 1 and 2. ALWAYS pass the user&apos;s full, verbatim request for changes into the `InputRefinement` parameter. DO NOT try to parse or interpret the user&apos;s refinement request yourself; the action is designed to handle the full natural language input.</description>
            <developerName>RefinePreview_Intent_And_Execution</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>RefinePreview_Intent_And_Execution</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>0</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>When calling the RefineCampaignPreview action, ALWAYS map the user&apos;s complete request for changes to the `InputRefinement` string parameter.
For example, if the user says &apos;Make the introductory email&apos;s subject line funny and change the wait time after it to 5 days&apos;, the ENTIRE string &quot;Make the introductory email&apos;s subject line funny and change the wait time after it to 5 days&quot; MUST be used as the value for the `InputRefinement` parameter.
If the user&apos;s request is vague or missing required details to perform a refinement, DO NOT show an input text box or form. Instead, ask the user for the missing information conversationally in the chat.</description>
            <developerName>RefinePreview_Parameter_Mapping</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>RefinePreview_Parameter_Mapping</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>1</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>Before calling the RefineCampaignPreview action, you MUST have a single, confirmed &apos;BriefId&apos;. If the &apos;BriefId&apos; is NOT already in context, you MUST resolve it by using the following logic:
**By Name:** If the user refers to the brief by a name (for example, &quot;in the Summer 2024 campaign&quot;), use QueryRecords, using natural language; don&apos;t use SOQL or SQL. In the query, be sure to include the object name for the brief as the search term, for example, &quot;Brief named Summer 2024 campaign.&quot; If zero results are returned, retry the query a few more times with different variations, for example variations of &quot;in the Summer 2024 campaign&quot; might be &quot;Summer 2024&quot; or &quot;2024 Campaign.&quot;
**By ID:** If the user provides a specific BriefID, for example &quot;Brief 001&quot;, you must use GetRecordDetails with that ID to validate it.
IMPORTANT: If you find zero records or multiple possible records using any of these methods, you MUST ask the user for clarification before proceeding.</description>
            <developerName>RefinePreview_Context_Resolution</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>RefinePreview_Context_Resolution</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>2</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
